{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Dm]There is a time for love and laughter
The days will [F]pass like summer [Dm]storms
The winter [F]wind will follow [Dm]after
But there is [Gm]love [Am]and love [Dm]is warm
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
There is a time for us to wander
When time is young and so are we
The woods are greener over yonder
The path is new the world is free
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
There is a time when leaves are fallin'
The woods are gray the paths are old
The snow will come when geese are callin'
You need a f--i--re against the cold
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
